/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  dimethylCarbonate-methylPhenylCarbonate -- AN NRTL PAIR FROM EVERY LABORATORY'S MEASUREMENTS.

  WRITTEN BY bin/choupo-curate pair methylPhenylCarbonate dimethylCarbonate (DEV.md 4c C284, the bulk run;
  record docs/design/binary-pairs-from-open-measurements.md section 11).

  THE DECLARATION -- WRITTEN AND COMMITTED BEFORE ANY FIT RAN (several
  declarations of the bulk run share one commit).

  IDENTITY.  methylPhenylCarbonate (CAS 13509-27-8, InChIKey XTBFPVLHGVYOQH-UHFFFAOYSA-N)
  + dimethylCarbonate (CAS 616-38-6, InChIKey IEJIGPNLZYLLBP-UHFFFAOYSA-N), joined
  to the archive through identity.json -- never by name.  CLASS (C284): both
  records are volatile molecular liquids (no role nonvolatile/solute, no
  dissociatesTo, no charge, no solid, a vapour-pressure model), and every
  measured temperature lies below both critical temperatures.

  NO MEASURED SERIES IN THIS TREE.  constant/archiveDatasets names each
  dataset (DOI, NIST URL, article sha256, extraction selector, extract
  sha256); `bin/choupo-curate fetch` writes the points into
  constant/archiveExtracts/, which is gitignored.

  STUDIES: every bubble-temperature block of the pair at or below 110 kPa
  with a declared uncertainty (1 block(s)).  FITTED, ALL OF THEM
  (1):
      10.1016/j.fluid.2013.09.030    block 9    20 pts  101.3 kPa  366.04-484.12 K  U 0.1-0.19 K
  SET ASIDE BY THE EXTRACTION RULES, BY NAME:
      (none)

  THE RULE (DEV.md 4c C283 amended, C284).  Every laboratory above is
  fitted; none is held out (the C16 partition and its band are retired as
  the acceptance test).  NRTL, a_ij = a_ji = 0, alpha = 0.30 fixed: two
  parameters (b_ij, b_ji); each point weighted by 1/U, U its own stated
  expanded uncertainty.  Objective twoStage (least squares, then minimax;
  T_bubble absolute, in K).  OUTLIERS: after a least-squares stage over every
  point, a point with |T_model - T| > 3 K is discarded BY
  NAME (`discard` on its evidence entry, listed below) and the fit repeated
  without it.
  THE GRADED ACCEPTANCE (DEV.md 4c C285, applied to pairs by C286): max
  |T_model - T| over the KEPT points is GRADED -- clean up to 1 K,
  warning up to 2 K, severe up to 4 K, refused above; a point with no
  bubble point refuses. C283's relative clause (5 / 10 / 20 %) judges
  composition; this fit has no composition residual, so only the
  temperature clause applies. Every grade but refused is accepted and
  promoted (autoPromoted, humanReviewed false) with `fitGrade` and its
  max |dT| in the record's provenance; the engine voices a warning or a
  severe grade on every run that reads the pair. A pair that splits ONE
  liquid inside its validity span is not promoted, whatever its grade
  (arm f).
  Two starts: (0, 0) and (800, -400).

  OUTLIERS DISCARDED AFTER THE LEAST-SQUARES STAGE:
  @@OUTLIERS-BEGIN@@
      2 point(s) of 20: doi 10.1016/j.fluid.2013.09.030 row 18: x 0.9858,
      P 101.300 kPa, T 475.80 K, dT +3.63 K; doi
      10.1016/j.fluid.2013.09.030 row 20: x 0.9963, P 101.300 kPa, T
      484.12 K, dT +4.19 K
  @@OUTLIERS-END@@

  @@MODELS-BEGIN@@
  THE OTHER ACTIVITY MODELS (DEV.md 4c C294), declared before their fits
  ran. The SAME datasets and the SAME kept points as fit_nrtl: each op
  below is fit_nrtl copied verbatim -- evidence, discards, objective,
  residual, weighting, options -- with only its parameters, its `thermo
  {}` fragment (the model) and its outputs changed; the outlier discard
  was decided ONCE, on the NRTL least-squares stage, and is reused, never
  re-decided per model. UNIQUAC: two parameters a_ij, a_ji (K), tau_ij =
  exp(-a_ij/T), b = c = 0 fixed (the NRTL default's count; temperature
  dependence 1/T), r and q each component's own record. Wilson: two
  parameters A_ij, A_ji (J/mol), Lambda_ij = (V_j/V_i) exp(-A_ij/RT), V
  the records' Vliq. Two starts each. Each model gets its own record
  (constant/parameters/<MODEL>/), its own grade at 1 / 2 / 4 K (max
  |T_model - T|), its own one-liquid test (arm f), `fitGradeBasis
  inSample`, the C300 cap and `review { by none; }`; a severe or refused
  grade, or a split, is not promoted. The three in-sample residuals are
  published side by side, never used to choose a model for the student.
  UNIQUAC: NOT FITTED -- methylPhenylCarbonate and dimethylCarbonate
  carry no UNIQUAC r and q (no tabulated value, and no UNIFAC groups to
  sum them from, bin/curate/uniquac_rq_from_groups.py) -- UNIQUAC is not
  fitted; nothing is estimated silently. Wilson: NOT FITTED --
  methylPhenylCarbonate carries no liquid molar volume Vliq, which
  Wilson's Lambda needs -- Wilson is not fitted.
  @@MODELS-END@@

  @@MODELS-RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE UNIQUAC AND WILSON FITS FOUND: neither was fitted. UNIQUAC:
  methylPhenylCarbonate and dimethylCarbonate carry no UNIQUAC r and q
  (no tabulated value, and no UNIFAC groups to sum them from,
  bin/curate/uniquac_rq_from_groups.py) -- UNIQUAC is not fitted; nothing
  is estimated silently. Wilson: methylPhenylCarbonate carries no liquid
  molar volume Vliq, which Wilson's Lambda needs -- Wilson is not fitted.
  @@MODELS-RESULT-END@@

  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  fit_nrtl: b_ij = -439.9 K, b_ji = 1126.2 K over 18 kept points of 1
  laboratories (2 discarded): max |dT| 2.649 K, mean 0.884 K, graded
  severe (limits 1 / 2 / 4 K) -> accepted. fit_nrtl_start2 lands on the
  same pair (-439.9, 1126.2). PROMOTED on 2026-11-12 into
  data/standards/parameters/NRTL/dimethylCarbonate-methylPhenylCarbonate.dat
  as reviewStatus autoPromoted, review by none, because: fit grade severe
  -- max |dT| 2.649 K over the 18 kept points, one liquid across the
  validity span; BEATS THE IDEAL MIXTURE (C334): 2.6485 K against ideal
  8.1463 K
  @@RESULT-END@@

  WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED.  The pair is correct at these pressures and in this
  frame (ideal-gas vapour, the catalogue's own vapour-pressure records); the
  measurements were transcribed by the archive and have NOT been read back
  against the articles (the CHECKLIST that `fetch` writes is the aid).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name        fit_nrtl;
        type        fitParameters;

        parameters
        (
            { path  equilibrium.liquid.activityModel.binaryParameters.methylPhenylCarbonate-dimethylCarbonate.b_ij;  initial 0;  min -3000;  max 3000; }
            { path  equilibrium.liquid.activityModel.binaryParameters.methylPhenylCarbonate-dimethylCarbonate.b_ji;  initial 0;  min -3000;  max 3000; }
        );

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset  "constant/archiveExtracts/methylPhenylCarbonate-dimethylCarbonate-bubble-j.fluid.2013.09.030.dat";
                role     fit;
                discard  ( 18 20 );   // C283 outliers, by name in the header
            }
        );

        objective { method twoStage;  scale { T_bubble absolute; } }
        residual
        {
            kind        T_bubble;
            components  ( methylPhenylCarbonate dimethylCarbonate );
            weighting   uncertainty;
        }

        options
        {
            maxIter      80;
            tolerance    1.0e-6;
            fdStep       1.0e-4;
            lambda0      1.0e-3;
        }

        output
        {
            fit_log    fit_history.csv;
            parity     parity.csv;
            proposal   dimethylCarbonate-methylPhenylCarbonate.proposal.dat;
        }
    }
    {
        name        fit_nrtl_start2;
        type        fitParameters;

        parameters
        (
            { path  equilibrium.liquid.activityModel.binaryParameters.methylPhenylCarbonate-dimethylCarbonate.b_ij;  initial 800;  min -3000;  max 3000; }
            { path  equilibrium.liquid.activityModel.binaryParameters.methylPhenylCarbonate-dimethylCarbonate.b_ji;  initial -400;  min -3000;  max 3000; }
        );

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset  "constant/archiveExtracts/methylPhenylCarbonate-dimethylCarbonate-bubble-j.fluid.2013.09.030.dat";
                role     fit;
                discard  ( 18 20 );   // C283 outliers, by name in the header
            }
        );

        objective { method twoStage;  scale { T_bubble absolute; } }
        residual
        {
            kind        T_bubble;
            components  ( methylPhenylCarbonate dimethylCarbonate );
            weighting   uncertainty;
        }

        options
        {
            maxIter      80;
            tolerance    1.0e-6;
            fdStep       1.0e-4;
            lambda0      1.0e-3;
        }

        output
        {
            parity     parity_start2.csv;
        }
    }
    {
        name        txy_ideal;
        type        propertyScan1D;
        vary        { variable x[methylPhenylCarbonate];  from 0.0;  to 1.0;  n 101; }
        state       { P 101.3 kPa;  composition { methylPhenylCarbonate 0.5;  dimethylCarbonate 0.5; } }
        thermo
        {
            equilibrium { liquid { activityModel { model ideal; } } }
        }
        properties  ( T_bubble  y_eq_methylPhenylCarbonate );
        output      { file txy_ideal.csv; }
    }
    {
        name        txy_nrtl;
        type        propertyScan1D;
        vary        { variable x[methylPhenylCarbonate];  from 0.0;  to 1.0;  n 101; }
        state       { P 101.3 kPa;  composition { methylPhenylCarbonate 0.5;  dimethylCarbonate 0.5; } }
        thermo
        {
            equilibrium { liquid { activityModel { model NRTL; /* no inline pair: the case's own record */ } } }
        }
        properties  ( T_bubble  y_eq_methylPhenylCarbonate );
        output      { file txy_nrtl.csv; }
    }
    // @@C294-OPS-BEGIN@@ -- UNIQUAC and Wilson on the NRTL fit's own evidence (DEV.md 4c C294)
    // @@C294-OPS-END@@
);

experimental
(
    {
        name      study1;
        component methylPhenylCarbonate;
        kind      txy;
        models    ( txy_ideal  txy_nrtl );
        dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/methylPhenylCarbonate-dimethylCarbonate-bubble-j.fluid.2013.09.030.dat";
        source    "IN-SAMPLE (fitted): doi 10.1016/j.fluid.2013.09.030";
    }
);
